Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["StructureAdaptiveEvolution", "ObjectName",
 CellID->93428065,ExpressionUUID->"01606214-a0a0-c444-b862-efd51548628a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"2c5ca5f0-6169-0741-8870-d0232097d83e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["StructureAdaptiveEvolution",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
StructureAdaptiveEvolution"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "opts", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8a8b8973-72b9-8143-8911-18110f661392"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "runs an adaptive multi-objective search over mutated hypergraph rewrite \
rules and returns a result association.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["StructureAdaptiveEvolution",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
StructureAdaptiveEvolution"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<Rule\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "rule"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<InitialState\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "state"}], ",", " ", 
     "opts"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "97319df5-eb3d-6646-9bd7-6bffad4aa6c8"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "searches from the seed rule or rule set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["rule", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0095de78-5406-654d-ae14-ae629538a9e8"],
 " and the initial hypergraph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["state", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0d85abf7-79f4-5c4f-bbad-c7213d8570ec"],
 ".",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
  "9da4b1b6-cee6-b34c-bcfa-b38be1903275"]
}], "Usage",
 CellID->544665961,ExpressionUUID->"bf6c465d-5a0e-b447-886f-41989b610cd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each round proposes \"MutationBudget\" candidates. A candidate is made by \
choosing a mutation strategy with probability given by the current strategy \
weights and applying it to a parent from an archive (the search front, \
per-objective champions and a few random valid candidates). Every candidate \
is evaluated once, by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
   "EvaluateCandidate", 
    "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/EvaluateCandidate", 
    "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/SamuelFrerichs/\
StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/EvaluateCandidate.html"},
   "TextRefLink",
   DisplayFunction->(TagBox[
     ButtonBox[
      StyleBox[#, ShowStringCharacters -> True, FontFamily -> 
       "Source Sans Pro"], 
      BaseStyle -> {"Link", FontColor -> LightDarkSwitched[
          RGBColor[0.02, 0.286, 0.651], 
          RGBColor[0.2823, 0.6666, 0.949]]}, ButtonData -> #2, ContentPadding -> 
      False], 
     MouseAppearanceTag["LinkHand"]]& )]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ad9398da-353d-544c-ad6e-02007c4b7d63"],
 ", with a canonical breadth-first multiway exploration under the evolution \
limits."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->90206089,ExpressionUUID->"3f77b9cc-9006-3a4e-aefb-277c7e7a5758"],

Cell["\<\
The search Pareto front is computed over the objective metrics of all valid \
candidates. The solution Pareto front contains only candidates that halted \
(status \"Halted\") and satisfy every hard constraint. The two archives are \
kept separate: a capped candidate can be on the search front but never on the \
solution front.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->573913094,ExpressionUUID->"cef6fc95-b05b-7a4f-ab0b-59b57dcd1850"],

Cell["\<\
The status is \"Halted\" when the exploration is exhaustive and found no \
cycle: it is verified to halt under this finite reachable exploration. \
\"CycleDetected\" means the explored states graph contains a cycle, so an \
infinite derivation exists; the result then carries a \"CycleWitness\". \
\"GenerationCap\", \"EventCap\", \"StateCap\" and \"TimedOut\" mean the \
exploration was not resolved within the stated limits, and \"Invalid\" means \
a rewrite application failed. A capped exploration never reports its \
unexplored frontier as terminal.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->726092860,ExpressionUUID->"922456e9-4031-3047-a867-ab241fa2995a"],

Cell["\<\
Evolution limits are an Association with the keys \"MaxGenerations\" (default \
10), \"MaxEvents\" (1000), \"MaxStates\" (Infinity) and \"TimeConstraint\" \
(30. seconds); missing keys take their defaults.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->699151210,ExpressionUUID->"63fbd50f-88db-5246-8470-074685df9638"],

Cell["\<\
Seed: \"Rule\" (a rule, a list of rules forming an unordered rule set, or \
Automatic for a rule from the Wolfram Physics Project registry) and \
\"InitialState\" (a hypergraph state, or Automatic). Search: \"Goal\" (a goal \
preset, default \"LargeFiniteTerminating\"), \"MutationStrategies\", \
\"StrategyOptions\", \"AdaptiveWeights\" (True; False keeps uniform weights, \
a random-mutation baseline), \"Rounds\" (1), \"MutationBudget\" (20), \
\"RandomSeed\".\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->718292666,ExpressionUUID->"c2bab3bc-1062-4c4a-88d0-2d6386f4604c"],

Cell["\<\
Metrics: \"FitnessMetrics\" (metric names; Automatic uses the preset), \
\"CustomFitnessMetrics\", \"MetricOverrides\" (promote or change the stage, \
direction, range, target, tolerance or threshold of a metric), \
\"MissingObjectivePolicy\" (\"Worst\", the default, or \"Exclude\"), \
\"CompromisePolicy\" (None or \"IdealPointDistance\"). A Target constraint \
requires an explicit \"Tolerance\"; a numeric Maximize or Minimize constraint \
requires a \"Threshold\".\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->64039827,ExpressionUUID->"7f07e3f7-badf-d24d-add1-6068f6a50338"],

Cell["\<\
Universe: \"EdgeSymmetry\" (\"Unordered\", \"Ordered\" or \"Declared\"), \
\"SymmetryGroups\", \"CanonicalForm\" (\"Exact\" or \"Native\"), \
\"RewriteSemantics\" (\"EdgeToken\" or \"VertexDeletion\"). Evaluation: \
\"EvolutionLimits\", \"EvolutionArtifacts\", \"UpdateOrder\", \
\"UpdateOrders\", \"Parallelization\" (False), \"InitialStateDiagnostics\" \
(\"Finalists\" or None), \"ReuseEvaluations\" (False), \"ResumeFrom\" (a \
previous result, to continue it exactly).\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->65117962,ExpressionUUID->"c48c5fe5-fb22-d54a-a39a-5fd5be641aeb"],

Cell["\<\
The result has the keys \"RunID\", \"Configuration\", \"Seed\", \"Baseline\", \
\"Candidates\", \"SearchParetoFront\", \"SolutionParetoFront\", \
\"FrontMembership\", \"FrontHistory\", \"MetricChampions\", \
\"SolutionChampions\", \"CompromiseCandidate\", \"InitialStateDiagnostics\", \
\"StrategyWeightHistory\", \"FinalStrategyWeights\", \"LineageEdges\", \
\"ProposalFailures\", \"RunLog\", \"Performance\", \"Provenance\" and \
\"ResumeState\".\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->706590269,ExpressionUUID->"51b6833d-8ff1-4e43-b037-d2f140b8a20a"],

Cell["\<\
Every candidate records its strategy, the exact mutation operators applied \
and the rule difference, its status and evidence, all fitness values, its \
runtime and its EvolutionKey and EvaluationID. \"Provenance\" records the run \
ID, start and end times, the Wolfram, paclet, Hypergraph and evaluator \
versions, the random seed, the state equivalence and the Registry code and \
version of a Registry seed.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->935970799,ExpressionUUID->"b92ac2de-ceaa-f149-8937-895136fac78a"],

Cell["\<\
In a formal model of this breadth-first canonical explorer, machine-checked \
in Lean 4 with Mathlib, a \"Halted\" status implies that every derivation \
from the initial state is finite and shorter than the number of explored \
states, and the longest derivation equals the longest path of the explored \
graph. This holds for a complete, invariant canonical form (the default \
\"Exact\" backend) and also when canonical forms are merely isomorphic copies \
(the \"Native\" backend). That this code implements the model is tested, not \
machine-checked.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->386179643,ExpressionUUID->"24525e4d-93d8-3a46-a30b-78ae8c54029f"]
}, Open  ]],

